.TH "RECORD\-TOTALS\.PY" "" "June 2026" ""
.SH "NAME"
\fBrecord\-totals\.py\fR
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBrecord\-totals\.py\fR
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
\fBrecord\-totals\.py\fR prints row or entity counts for the RECORD provenance database\. The output format depends on the configured backend:
.P
\fBRelational backends (SQLite, PostgreSQL):\fR
.P
Queries every table in the \fBpublic\fR schema and prints the row count for each table, followed by a grand total\. Table names and counts are printed to standard output as they are retrieved\. Any table that cannot be counted (e\.g\. due to a permissions error) produces a warning on standard error and is skipped\.
.P
\fBGremlin backend:\fR
.P
Prints a breakdown of vertex counts grouped and sorted by label, then the total vertex count, followed by the same for edges\. The label breakdown is printed as a side effect of the count queries\.
.SH "OPTIONS"
This script accepts no options or arguments\. The schema name for relational backends is hard\-coded as \fBpublic\fR\.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
Returns 0 on success\.
.P
Returns non\-zero if:
.IP "\(bu" 4
the \fBrecord\fR library cannot be imported from \fBlib/\fR; or
.IP "\(bu" 4
a database connection error occurs\.
.IP "" 0
.P
Individual table count failures are non\-fatal and produce warnings on standard error rather than a non\-zero exit\.
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
The script inherits all database connection environment variables from the \fBrecord\fR library\. Refer to \fBrecord\.py\fR for the full list, including:
.TP
\fBRECORD_DBTYPE\fR
Selects the database backend\. One of \fBsqlite3\fR, \fBpostgres\fR, or \fBgremlin\fR\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_DBFILE\fR
Path to the SQLite database file\. Used when \fBRECORD_DBTYPE\fR is \fBsqlite3\fR\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_DBUSER\fR
PostgreSQL username\. Used when \fBRECORD_DBTYPE\fR is \fBpostgres\fR\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_DBNAME\fR
PostgreSQL database name\. Used when \fBRECORD_DBTYPE\fR is \fBpostgres\fR\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_POSTGRES_HOST\fR
PostgreSQL hostname\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_POSTGRES_PORT\fR
PostgreSQL port number\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_POSTGRES_PASSWORD\fR
PostgreSQL password\. Required when \fBRECORD_DBTYPE\fR is \fBpostgres\fR\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_GREMLIN_HOST\fR
WebSocket URL of the Gremlin server\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_GREMLIN_TIMEOUT\fR
Per\-query evaluation timeout in milliseconds\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_DEBUG\fR
When set, enables verbose diagnostic output to standard error\.
.SH "RETURN VALUE"
For relational backends, prints output of the form:
.IP "" 4
.nf
Found <n> tables in schema 'public'
<table_name>: <row_count>
\|\.\|\.\|\.
Grand total rows across all tables in 'public': <total>
.fi
.IP "" 0
.P
For the Gremlin backend, prints output of the form:
.IP "" 4
.nf
[{'<label>': <count>, \|\.\|\.\|\.}]
There are [<total>] vertices\.
[{'<label>': <count>, \|\.\|\.\|\.}]
There are [<total>] edges\.
.fi
.IP "" 0
.SH "EXAMPLES"
Print row counts for a PostgreSQL or SQLite database:
.IP "" 4
.nf
record\-totals\.py
.fi
.IP "" 0
.P
Print vertex and edge counts for a Gremlin database:
.IP "" 4
.nf
RECORD_DBTYPE=gremlin record\-totals\.py
.fi
.IP "" 0
.SH "FILES"
.TP
\fBlib/record\.py\fR
The RECORD provenance library\. Must be importable as \fBrecord\fR; the script appends \fBlib\fR to \fBsys\.path\fR before importing, so \fBrecord\.py\fR must be present in a \fBlib/\fR subdirectory relative to the working directory\.
