.SH "BUGS"
Debug output is unconditionally enabled by \fBrecord\.debug = True\fR at module level in \fBrecord\.py\fR and cannot be suppressed via the \fBRECORD_DEBUG\fR environment variable\.
.P
The schema name \fBpublic\fR is hard\-coded in the \fB__main__\fR block and cannot be overridden without editing the script\. The \fBget_table_names\fR and \fBcount_total_rows\fR functions accept a \fBschema\fR parameter but it is never exposed to the user\.
.P
\fBget_table_names\fR uses \fBpg_catalog\fR and is therefore PostgreSQL\-specific\. When \fBRECORD_DBTYPE\fR is \fBsqlite3\fR, the relational branch will call this function and it will fail, as SQLite does not have a \fBpg_catalog\fR schema\. The SQLite backend is therefore not supported by this script despite appearing to be\.
.P
The \fBget_vertices\fR and \fBget_edges\fR functions print the label\-grouped breakdown as a side effect via \fBprint(result)\fR rather than returning it\. This mixes display logic with data retrieval and makes the functions difficult to reuse\.
.P
The \fBget_nodes_by_label\fR function is defined but its only call site is commented out in \fB__main__\fR, so it is currently unused\.
.P
The Gremlin vertex and edge count queries use a hard\-coded evaluation timeout of 1,200,000 milliseconds (20 minutes) via \fBg\.with(\|\.\|\.\|\.)\fR, which ignores the \fBRECORD_GREMLIN_TIMEOUT\fR environment variable\.
.P
The \fBcount_rows_in_table\fR function uses an f\-string to construct a \fBWITH\fR cursor block, but \fBconn\.cursor()\fR as a context manager requires the database driver to support it; this will fail with drivers that do not implement \fB__exit__\fR on cursors\.
